BT /F1 9 Tf 40 750 Td 14 TL (FIRST INFORMATION REPORT \(Under Section 154 Cr.P.C. / Section 173 BNSS, 2023\)) ' (POLICE STATION: Economic Offences Wing \(EOW\), Mandir Marg, New Delhi) ' (DISTRICT: New Delhi | YEAR: 2024 | FIR NO: 0412/2024 | DATE & TIME: 14/08/2024 at 11:30 AM) ' (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) ' (1. ACTS & STATUTORY SECTIONS CITED:) ' (   \(a\) Section 420 Indian Penal Code / Sec 318 BNS \(Cheating & Dishonestly Inducing Delivery\)) ' (   \(b\) Section 406 Indian Penal Code / Sec 316 BNS \(Criminal Breach of Trust\)) ' (   \(c\) Section 468 & 471 Indian Penal Code / Sec 336 & 340 BNS \(Forgery for Cheating & Using Forged Document\)) ' (   \(d\) Section 323 & 506 Indian Penal Code / Sec 115 & 351 BNS \(Voluntarily Causing Hurt & Intimidation\)) ' (   \(e\) Section 120-B Indian Penal Code / Sec 61 BNS \(Criminal Conspiracy\)) ' (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) ' (2. COMPLAINANT INFORMATION:) ' (   Name: Mr. Vikramaditya Singhania, Managing Director, Apex FinTech Innovations Ltd.) ' (   Registered Office: Cyber City, Tower B, Level 14, Gurugram, NCR.) ' (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) ' (3. ACCUSED PERSONS:) ' (   Accused No. 1: Rajesh Malhotra, Managing Director, Zenith Cloud Technologies Pvt. Ltd.) ' (   Accused No. 2: Sameer Verma, Chief Technical Officer, Zenith Cloud Technologies Pvt. Ltd.) ' (   Accused No. 3: M/s Zenith Cloud Technologies Pvt. Ltd., Okhla Industrial Area Ph-III, New Delhi.) ' (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) ' (4. STATEMENT OF FACTS AND ALLEGATIONS:) ' (The Complainant company entered into a Master Software Deployment and Escrow Agreement on 15/01/2024) ' (with Zenith Cloud Technologies Pvt. Ltd. for implementing a high-throughput algorithmic core clearing engine.) ' (The total agreed contractual consideration was INR 8,50,00,000/- \(Eight Crores Fifty Lakhs Only\).) ' (Under Clause 3.2 of the agreement, Complainant released Milestone Tranche-1 of INR 4,25,00,000/- on 05/02/2024.) ' (This disbursement was made strictly upon Accused No. 1 and 2 furnishing an ISO/IEC 27001 Security Audit) ' (Certificate and Third-Party Escrow Confirmation purportedly issued by CertiGuard Labs Singapore on 04/02/2024.) ' () ' (In July 2024, when milestone delivery was overdue, an internal technical audit revealed that CertiGuard Labs) ' (was a fictitious entity registered in Delaware by a close relative of Accused No. 1.) ' (No proprietary source code was ever deposited into the independent third-party escrow repository.) ' (Bank verification revealed that within 48 hours of credit, INR 4,10,00,000/- was systematically diverted) ' (to personal demat accounts and an affiliated real estate shell company, Malhotra Ventures LLP.) ' (On 10/08/2024, when Complainant visited the Okhla premises to demand inspection of code, Accused No. 1) ' (physically assaulted Complainant's officers, caused severe bodily injuries, threatened criminal intimidation,) ' (and bolted the office doors to prevent escape.) ' () ' (5. PRIMA FACIE FINDINGS OF INVESTIGATING OFFICER:) ' (The accused persons dishonestly induced the complainant to part with INR 4,25,00,000/- using forged credentials.) ' (Ingredients of cheating under Section 420 IPC and criminal breach of trust under Section 406 IPC are attracted.) ' ET
endstream
